    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1326">

                <pb facs="1586" n="1388" xml:id="pg1388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Pauley
                    Files</note>
                <head>No. 1326<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Deputy Military Governor, United States Zone in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Clay</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1326-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-04">August 4, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for General Clay</hi></p>
                <p>At a meeting of The Big Three Conference the United States introduced a
                        proposal<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1326-f2"/> in which the Soviet Government was
                    asked to deliver from Rumania, Hungary and Austria 50,000 barrels of crude oil
                    or refined oil products per day into the Western Zone of Occupation beginning
                    September 1, 1945. This introduction was made at the request of the Army and the
                    Petroleum Administration for War and referred to
                    the Economic Subcommittee of which I was a member. Although we pushed this to
                    the greatest extent we received no affirmative answer from the Soviet
                    Government.</p>
                <p>The Soviet representatives in their last report to The Big Three made the
                    following official report:<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1326-f3"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Soviet representatives indicate that they have not yet received full
                            information as to such possibility, although their preliminary data
                            suggest the absence of any substantial surplus in the producing areas.
                            They indicate that they will explore the matter further and report at a
                            later date.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
